    "intro_html":  "Dirty rice earns its name honestly. The rice turns brown because chicken livers and browned meat get cooked into it, and that is where all the depth comes from. Onion, celery, and green bell pepper form the Cajun holy trinity, bacon starts the pan, and turkey carries the protein. Each serving lands at 657 calories with \u003cstrong\u003e43 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$3.25\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). Louisiana has been feeding people well on cheap cuts for three hundred years and it shows.",
